  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Net Zero World Renewable Energy Mini Grids Feasibility Study, through tQAutomation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant funds a feasibility study (FS) for Perusahaan Listrik Negara (PLN), a state-owned Indonesian utility, to assess the technical and economic viability of converting diesel-based generation in five target locations in eastern Indonesia to renewable energy (RE) based mini grids. The study will also develop a roadmap and replication strategy to replace up to 499 Megawatts (MW) of small diesel generation with RE mini grids in approximately one quarter of the frontier, outermost and least developed (Terluar, Terpencil, Tertinggal (3T)) regions of Indonesia. The FS would help PLN address growing electricity demand and reduce reliance on fossil fuel-based power generation.</narrative>
  </description>
